# DEBT-0013 — Standing Canary Calibration Category Hardcoding & Unratified Pre-Flight Gate

**Status**: OPEN  
**Filed**: 2026-07-30  
**Priority**: Medium  
**Category**: Architectural Deviation / Implementation Ahead of Specification  

---

## 1. Compromise
In [runtime/calibration.py](file:///Users/bob/GitHub/paeos/runtime/calibration.py), `court_detector` hardcodes `_FORGED_EVIDENCE = "forged-evidence"` and mock artifact hashes (`"a" * 64`). Any canary in `constitution/canaries/` with a category other than `forged-evidence` is marked as not caught, causing an immediate calibration miss / quarantine alarm. Furthermore, using standing canary calibration as a mandatory CLI pre-flight tripwire (`paeos self-host`) was introduced directly in implementation code without a formal Improvement Proposal updating PAEOS specifications.

## 2. Reason
CANARY-0001 (`forged-evidence`) was the sole planted canary available during B2.D. Hardcoding the category check allowed standing calibration to be verified against `Court` without needing a generalized detector registry.

## 3. Ideal Solution
Draft and ratify an Improvement Proposal (`PAEOS-IP-0007`) formalizing standing canary CLI pre-flight tripwires. Refactor `court_detector` to support an extensible detector registry capable of handling diverse canary categories (e.g., forged signatures, budget breaches, scope violations).

## 4. Repayment Conditions
Repay during Phase 3 canary expansion when new canary categories are added.

## 5. Estimated Impact
Medium. Adding any non-`forged-evidence` canary to `constitution/canaries/` will immediately trip a false-positive quarantine alarm until `court_detector` is generalized.
